A held note ends on the track an input stops reaching (Segno). Applies after per-track-inputs.

When a MIDI input's destination went (the live input following the selection to another track,
an input changed), its held notes were sent as note-offs to the tracks it still reached, cutting
notes there, while the track it left kept them sounding for good. Now they go to that track only.
A destination whose monitoring turns off, or whose channel filter ("fdChannel") changes, ends the
held notes it no longer hears on its track.

